<title>USA: US ruling on FDA's tobacco role seen after Mar 24.</title>
<headline>US ruling on FDA's tobacco role seen after Mar 24.</headline>
<dateline>GREENSBORO, N.C. 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The federal judge overseeing the tobacco industry's challenge to proposed Food and Drug Administration regulation of the sale and marketing of cigarettes will not rule before March 24, a court clerk said on Monday.</p>
<p>U.S. District Judge William Osteen Sr. in Greensboro had taken the case under advisement after a hearing on February 10.</p>
<p>The hearing concerned the tobacco industry's motion for summary judgment in which the judge has been asked to make a decision on the merits of the case without a trial.</p>
</text>
